"origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about places in a limited range of social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "structure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something large that is built", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is an important structure in China.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about places in China.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "The Great Wall of China ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a stone wall built across northern China", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: On my trip, I visited The Great Wall of China.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "capital city ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the city in a country where their government is ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The guards sent signals to the capital city. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dynasty ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a period of time when a particular family ruled a country", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The emperors were a part of the Ming Dynasty.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "state ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an area that makes up a part of a country ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The first step was to connect the walls between the different states.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "emperor ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the man who is the ruler of an empire", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Emperors helped build the wall.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Saying How Far a Place Is", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to know how far a place is, you can ask the question: <span class=\"italic\">How far is\u2026 ?</span> / <span class=\"italic\">How far is \u2026 from here? </span><br/><br/>You can reply with a specific distance if you know the answer, like <span class=\"italic\">It's 50 yards away</span>.<br/><br/>In the USA, you use the Imperial system, not the metric system. <br/><br/>If a place is nearby, you use yards to say how far it is. <br/><br/>If a place is far, you use miles to say how far it is. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: How far is the end of the wall from here? <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Guide</span>: It's 4,000 miles away.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Imperial System</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Metric System</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 1 mile\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 1.6 kilometers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 1 yard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 90 centimeters\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"1 foot\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 30 centimeters\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 1 inch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 2.5 centimeters\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You can use the Simple Present tense to say how far a place is. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Simple Past Tense ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you travel, you ask and report about things you see. You can use the Simple Past tense to report about the things you see. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Who built this?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Remember, there are regular and irregular verbs. <br/> You use Wh-questions to ask about places you visit. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Why did you decide to visit the Great Wall?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I visited the Great Wall of China.", "type"